From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:38:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] luks_disk: a driver for decrypted LUKS2 devices

drivers/disk/virtual/luks_disk publishes each LUKS2 volume opened with
its volume key as /dev/disk/virtual/luks/<id>/raw, which the disk device
manager scans and file systems mount like any disk. It is opened and closed
through ioctls on /dev/disk/virtual/luks/control (the luks command runs the
KDF in userland), or at boot through its boot module. Every key is checked
against the header's digest; closing is refused while a file system on it
is mounted, and the key is wiped when the last descriptor is closed.

Reads and writes go through a fixed pool of bounce buffers per device, so
writing back pages never needs an allocation; partial sectors are
read-modified-written under a lock; flushes are passed down, discards are
not. The driver is in the haiku package and its boot module set.

Tested in QEMU (x86_64, UEFI, NVMe): src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/
run-driver-test.sh, 30 checks in Haiku and 5 on the build host against
cryptsetup's volumes and keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
